# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Visual Design Guide

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-VISUAL-DESIGN-GUIDE.md`  
**Authority:** Level 5 — visual design system.

## Hard requirement

All UI must use the **Transovo design system** — tokens, typography scale, spacing, semantic colors, radii, shadows, density. Read the full guide before styling.

## Non-negotiables

- **No arbitrary** font sizes, padding, colors, radii, or shadows on individual pages.
- Consume **shared tokens** (`src/styles/kimi/`, design-system components).
- **Button hierarchy** is consistent: primary / secondary / destructive / ghost.
- **Status colors** are semantic — not decoration-only.
- Kimi surfaces must **not** redesign independently — design within the system.
- Light mode is primary; dark behavior follows guide if enabled.

## On conflict

Governance and page architecture win over visual preference. Full doc wins over this summary.
